 to recognize that  global health inequalities as well as  national health inequalities are a  danger to all of us and so as party  leader I'm proud of our members proud of  the way we've developed  great greater democracy in the party and  some of the more democratic procedures  that have been introduced but clearly  there's a long way to go you talk there  about changing the agenda means which of  the leadership contenders do you think  is best place to continue your legacy  listen they vote they fought a good  campaign they've had great debates all  of them I know them all very well at  various times they've all been in the  shadow cabinet  they've all been appointed by me some  resigned another student to resigned and  one didn't say is should we conclude  that the one who didn't ensure what you  should conclude is that I am determined  that our party remains an anti-austerity  party remains dedicated increasing human  rights away if you're in labor member  trying to work out who the best person  is to do that what would you say to them  what would save them is think through  what you want for our party in our  society think through who's going to  carry forward the anti austerity agenda  but think through also the needs of  strengthened democracy within our party  and I tell you what I'm going to be very  busy doing campaigning work on economy  on human rights and environmental issues  I am NOT disappearing from anywhere if  you're not disappearing is there a  particular Shadow Cabinet role that you  got your eye on well I've always spent  my life trying to deal with issues of  human rights and justice around the  world and that is something whether I  have a position or not is not important  what's important is that we use the  honor of holding public office to hold  executives to account but also to hold  the unaccountable to account for those  that are fighting their human rights  shadow for a secretary are you  suggesting something Jeremy Corbyn thank  you very much thank you very program  today thank you
 

